                <pb facs="0127" n="117" xml:id="pg117"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/1436: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-27">December 27, 1941</date>.<lb/>[Received December
                        27—4:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>335. Department’s circular December 8, 1 a.m. President informed me this morning
                    that Cabinet decided yesterday to suspend as from today all cable and radio
                    communication between Venezuela and non-American countries.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
